---
description: Объединить исходники 1С выбранных веток без переноса спеков и прочих файлов
agent: code
---

Use this command only from an active ready `itldev/*` worktree. A single branch name selects pair synchronization. For several branches or an explicit `-BranchSyncRequestPath`, use the group request below. Infer the named sources and final recipients from the user's authorized scope; ask only if that scope is missing.

Run the monitored helper directly from the current project directory with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` when supported:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action sync-dev-branches -PeerDevBranchName "<other-dev-branch-name>"
```

For a group, write a UTF-8 JSON request under the current project's ignored
`.agent-1c/source-sync/` directory with `schemaVersion: 1`, `peers` (an array of
the other branch names), and `recipients` (an array of the explicitly selected
final recipients, including the current branch). Run the same monitored helper
with `-Action sync-dev-branches -BranchSyncRequestPath "<absolute-request-path>"`
instead of `-PeerDevBranchName`. Do not emulate a group with successive pair
commands: earlier peers would miss later inputs. The helper first composes and
validates the complete result, then delivers it to every selected recipient and
loads each recipient's database. Source-only participants receive no combined
source transfer or database load. Details and a JSON example are in
`references/branch-lifecycle.md`, "Group source synchronization".

The helper checkpoints both branches, combines only `src/cf/**` for configuration branches or the same `src/cfe/<extension>/**` for extension branches, preserves each branch's own `ConfigDumpInfo.xml`, and loads the combined result into both branch infobases. It never transfers specs, tests, documentation, workflow files, or any other repository paths. The branches receive independent source-only commits, so neither branch becomes a Git ancestor of the other.

If source conflicts created by this synchronization are reported, resolve only the listed 1C source files, run `git add`, and repeat the same command from the same branch. Do not create the synchronization commit manually.

For a group interruption, retain and repeat the exact request. The durable plan
reports each participant's pinned source, source delivery and database load.
The helper reconciles saved commits and successful load receipts instead of
replaying them. `DEV_BRANCH_SOURCE_SYNC_LOAD_UNCONFIRMED` is an unresolved native
outcome: follow the database recovery diagnostics, preserve the plan, and never
edit its statuses or manufacture a receipt to unblock it.

If `DEV_BRANCH_SOURCE_SYNC_PENDING_REFRESH` is reported, do not stop after describing the peer as blocked. Follow `requiredAction` in the same task: move to the exact reported worktree and continue its original `/itl-refresh` or `/itl-refresh-lite` wrapper. Use progressive semantic repair there: start with the listed semantic units, preserve every compatible delta, run the directly relevant validators, stage the repair, and repeat the same refresh wrapper. Widen to related source, history, tests, OpenSpec, and required product documentation only for a concrete uncertainty or failed check. Ask the user only when authoritative evidence still leaves incompatible business outcomes; give exact options, consequences, and a recommendation. Never abort the merge, edit lifecycle state, or create its merge commit manually. After the refresh succeeds, return to the original worktree and repeat this synchronization automatically. When an existing agent task actively owns the peer worktree and the client can continue it, send that task the exact recovery and wait for its result; otherwise perform the recovery directly without editing concurrently with another task.

For `DEV_BRANCH_SOURCE_SYNC_PENDING_LIFECYCLE`, ask the concrete operation-level question from `requiredAction`; synchronization must not replace a different pending lifecycle operation. An unowned or inconsistent Git operation remains fail-closed. On success with a non-empty `userReport`, return it exactly as Russian Markdown. On any other failure, follow `requiredAction`; read only the last 80 lines of `logPath` for an unclassified runner failure.
